      "text": "Settings\n\nGeneral\n\nReading\n\nAI\n\nPlugins\n\nTheme\n\nCustomize\n\nShortcuts\n\nData & Sync\n\nAbout\n\nRSS Reader\n\nSentence Reader\n\nTTS Voices\n\nWebDAV Sync\n\nData & Sync\nReadAware is local-first: your data lives on this device. Sync is an encrypted relay, not a source of truth.\nSync\nSync backend\nWebDAV · via the webdav-sync plugin\nDisconnect\nStatus\nLast synced 3:13:55 PM\nSync now\nEnd-to-end encryption\nOn — protected by your passphrase.\nStorage\nData location\n/Users/ahpx/Library/Application Support/com.readaware.app.sync-acceptance-20260913-b\nReveal\nBackup & export\nChoose a complete encrypted backup or a library backup.\n\nExport a backup\nBooks, annotations, conversations, memory, settings, plugins and credentials, saved with password encryption.\nExport\nRestore a backup\nOpen an encrypted full backup, compare it with this library, and choose what to restore. Your current device identity and account session stay on this device.\nImport\nContext bundles\nVersioned, reproducible context artifacts for external agents: the reader profile, declared reading intentions, one book's memory behind the current spoiler boundary, or one conversation's stored summary. Each capture publishes an immutable version to your synced event log; saving writes a JSON file you choose.\n\nRecipe\n\nReader profile\nScope\n\nThis reader\nCapture now\nReads the current sources and publishes a new version only when the content changed.\nCapture\nVersions\nNewest first. Saving writes the exact published artifact.\nNo versions yet.\nDanger zone\nDelete all data\nErase everything on this device — books, annotations, reading history, settings, and sync credentials. A synced account's copy on other devices is not touched.\nDelete all data\n"
